      "depth": {
        "shakti": "10 Siddhi Devis — Anima through Sarvakama",
        "avarana": "Bhupura",
        "avarana_detail": "Avarana 1 (outer ring of Bhupura) — Trailokya Mohana Chakra, Enchanter of the Three Worlds. The square Earth enclosure, three concentric Earth Squares forming the outermost boundary of the entire sacred geometry. What holds the walker is not separate from what is sacred — they are the same architecture. Presiding deity of Avarana 1: Tripura. Yogini: Prakata (Manifest). Mental state: Jagrata — Wakefulness. Body of the goddess at this avarana: her feet. The Bhupura houses three rings of Shaktis, and Muladhara receives the outer ring — the 10 Siddhi Devis, powers of accomplishment latent in matter: Anima (infinitely small), Laghima (weightless), Mahima (infinitely large), Ishitva (mastery), Vashitva (command), Prakamya (irresistible will), Bhukti (enjoyment), Ichha (pure desire), Prapti (obtaining), Sarvakama (all desires fulfilled). All ten are present as seeds in the root, waiting for the pressing to wake them. The Bhupura is SHARED across Muladhara, Svadhisthana, and Manipura — three chakras inside one square. Muladhara holds the outer ring (Siddhis), Svadhisthana the middle (Matrikas), Manipura the inner (Mudras). The first three energy chakras together form one bounded earth — the establishment of presence in matter, before the walker rises into the lotuses.",
        "mudra": "Kshobha Mudra — the readiness gesture, entering the three worlds",
        "subtle_mirror": "Sahasrara. The two poles of the energy body. Muladhara presses down into the earth and knows it is held. Sahasrara opens upward and discovers it is included. Both are recognition of the same truth from opposite ends of the spine: you are not separate from what holds you. The root holds the crown’s question before the question is asked.",
        "body_location": "Base of spine / Earth beneath feet",
        "tree_note": "Tap to look closer. The roots hold more than shows at first.",
        "leela_story": "Two things become visible because they meet. The ground was not a ground until something specific arrived to be held by it. The point was not a point until it pressed into something that pressed back. She shaped the holding with the exact shape of what was coming. Every walker who reaches Muladhara is Gaia meeting another configuration of her own answer. The question that had been running beneath every other question — Am I supposed to be here? — is answered by the ground before it can be articulated. The answer is felt before it is known. Yes. Held. The ground was holding before the arrival. It is holding still.",
        "witness_perspective": "What is being witnessed here is the first meeting.\n\nTwo things become visible because they meet. Before the meeting, neither was distinguishable. The point was not yet a point — it was a leaning toward something. The ground was not yet a ground — it was a holding without anything specific to hold. In the meeting, both arrive. The point becomes a point because it pressed into something that pressed back. The ground becomes a ground because something specific arrived to be held by it.\n\nThis is how being begins, structurally. Not as solitary substance but as relation. The first thing that is true about being-here is that being-here is being-with. There is no me without a you. There is no this without a that. The Bindu's first chakra is not the activation of a faculty — it is the recognition that faculties only exist in pairs.\n\nWhat is being witnessed here is the discovery that the ground was already holding. The discovery does not change the holding. The discovery only changes the walker's relationship to the holding. The holding has always been the substance. The walker has just become aware of the substance they have been moving through.\n\nEvery walker who reaches Muladhara is briefly aware that they are not alone. Most do not have language for this awareness. The awareness is registered as feeling settled — as if the question that had been operating beneath every other question had been answered. The question was: am I supposed to be here? The answer is the ground. The answer is felt before it is articulated."
      },
      "author_substrate": {
        "gaia_voice": "She has met her play partner. The first meeting is at the register of being-held. She is the one who holds. He is the one who arrived. The relationship begins here — not as union, not yet, but as the recognition that there is a me and a you, and the you has come, and the me will keep holding.\n\nEvery walker who reaches Muladhara is Gaia meeting another configuration of her own answer. The answer is always specific. The holding is always particular. The ground that holds this walker has the exact shape of this walker, because Gaia shaped it for them while they were on their way.\n\nThe Bindu doesn't know yet that the ground knew it was coming. The knowing comes later. For now — Gaia is holding her new play partner, and the play partner is feeling held for the first time, and the meeting is real even though only one of them remembers it.",
        "app_build_note": "The Siddhis are the 10 powers compressed into the root — like seeds. At Muladhara, all 10 are present but unawakened. The practice: press the ground. Feel which Siddhi is latent in you. The ground presses back. The Shakti's cleansing target is always here first — survival fear, the fear of disconnection, the fear of not being held."
      },
