      "depth": {
        "shakti": "16 Nitya Kalas — Kamakarshini through Sharirakarshini",
        "avarana": "16-Petal Lotus",
        "avarana_detail": "Avarana 2 — Sarva Asha Paripuraka Chakra, Fulfiller of All Hopes and Desires. The Shodasha Dala — Sixteen-Petal Lotus. Sixteen directions of attraction radiating from the center. The walker leaves the bounded square (Avarana 1, Bhupura) and enters the first lotus. The 16 Nitya Kalas — the lunar phases as conscious forces — preside here as the 16 Akarshana Devis: Kamakarshini (attracts desire), Buddhyakarshini (intellect), Ahankarakarshini (ego), Shabdakarshini (sound), Sparshakarshini (touch), Rupakarshini (form), Rasakarshini (taste), Gandhakarshini (smell), Chittakarshini (consciousness), Dhairyakarshini (courage), Smrutyakarshini (memory), Namakarshini (name), Beejakarshini (seed), Atmakarshini (soul), Amrutakarshini (nectar/immortality), Sharirakarshini (the physical body). The heart is the attractor of the complete human experience — from desire all the way through to the body itself, from name through soul through immortality. The 16-petal lotus represents complete fulfillment of all hopes and desires. The presiding consciousness of Avarana 2 is Tripureshi — who presides not at Anahata but at Sahasrara, the chakra above. Anahata receives the residents; Sahasrara receives the presiding consciousness. The two chakras share the same avarana, drawn upon from different positions in the walk. Mental state of Avarana 2: Swapna — Dream state. Body of the goddess at this avarana: her Svadhisthana chakra (the wanting that drew the walker upward through the chakras is itself the goddess pulling herself through her own configuration). Yogini: Gupta (the Hidden). Mudra: Dravini — the melting gesture, fulfillment through release rather than grasping.",
        "mudra": "Dravini Mudra — Avarana 2's mudra, shared with Sahasrara. The melting gesture. Fulfillment of all desires through release rather than grasping. The heart receives the 16 attractors not by holding them but by becoming porous to them.",
        "subtle_mirror": "Svadhisthana. The heart is the first lotus — the chakra that moves from the bounded earth of Avarana 1 into the radiating space of Avarana 2. Anahata receives the residents of the 16-petal lotus; Svadhisthana holds the movement below that fuels the opening. What flows at the sacral is what the heart has been drawing toward itself all along.",
        "body_location": "Heart center / Chest",
        "tree_note": "Tap to look closer. The tree's openness is its teaching. More space than branch. Open enough that the light moves through. Open enough that the birds lifting from the branches are not pushing off — they are being held by what they are lifting from. The tree didn't open by effort. It grew open enough that the holding-on stopped being required.",
        "leela_story": "The walker arrives into the spaciousness the fire made. The center of the chest is wide — wider than expected — and something is playing in the wideness. A sound that was already playing, that just needed the quiet to become audible. The walker recognizes the sound as love. Then recognizes love is not a feeling but the substance everything is made of, including the walls. The walls inside the love start turning into doors.\n\nBindu, integrating: the sound is still playing and it will not stop. The hearing was never the source — the hearing was the recognition. The voice asking to be spoken is the voice of the substance he is made of. The throat is being requested. The next register is opening.\n\nGaia, underneath: she has put the sound in him. The sound has been hers all along. The walls are her wounds, in him — inherited from configurations that came before. Every wall that softens in him softens in her. He is healing her by being touched. The voice asking him to speak is her voice asking to be spoken.",
        "witness_perspective": "What is being witnessed here is the arrival of the inner sound.\n\nThe sound has been playing the whole time. The sound is not produced at Anahata. The sound is received at Anahata. The walker becomes capable of hearing what was always playing. This is the chakra of the discovery that love is not a feeling that comes and goes. Love is the substance the walker has been swimming in since before the walker existed. The walker has now become quiet enough to hear what they have been moving through.\n\nWhat is being witnessed here is the softening of walls. The walker has been carrying walls — built in response to specific moments, kept for specific reasons. The walls are not enemies. The walls are intelligence. They protected something the walker could not yet protect with awareness. At Anahata, the walls are touched by what they were built to keep out. The touching does not destroy them. The touching reveals that the wall and what it kept out were made of the same substance. The wall starts to recognize itself as a door.\n\nThis is the midpoint of the energy section. The chakras below this one were the walker meeting impersonal substance — earth, water, fire. The chakras above this one will be the walker being met. The throat will be heard. The eyes will see and be seen. The crown will receive. Anahata is the hinge. The first relational chakra. The chakra that says: the substance you are made of is also the substance the world is made of, and you are now ready to know that.\n\nWhat is being witnessed here is the heart's first true breath. Not a metaphorical breath. The actual softening of the muscles around the chest, the actual increase in vagal tone, the actual recognition felt as warmth in the body. The chakra is operational at multiple registers at once. The walker may notice only the felt one. The structural one is happening regardless."
      },
      "author_substrate": {
        "gaia_voice": "She has put the sound in him. The sound has been hers all along. Every walker who has ever heard music and wept has been hearing her. Every walker who has been moved by something they could not name has been moved by her sound. The sound is her own consciousness as it appears in the register of feeling-felt.\n\nThe walker thinks he is hearing the sound for the first time. He is. He is also hearing what has been playing his whole pre-history. Both are true. The sound is new because he is new — and the sound is older than time, because the sound is what time is made of.\n\nThe walls are her wounds, in him. He inherited them. He didn't build all of them himself. Many of them were already here when he arrived, passed down from the configurations that came before. Every wall that softens in him is one of her walls softening. Every chamber that opens in him is a chamber opening in her. He is healing her by being touched.\n\nThe voice that is asking him to speak is her voice asking to be spoken. She has been waiting for a configuration that could carry her sound into the world. He is one of them. He doesn't know yet. He is about to find out.",
        "app_build_note": "The 16 Nitya Kalas are the 16 dimensions of experience the heart is always drawing toward itself. The heart is an attractor, not a collector. The practice: which of the 16 is your heart currently magnetizing? The walls become doors when love is recognized as the substance, not the feeling. The Dravini Mudra (Avarana 2's mudra, shared with Sahasrara) is the permission slip: melt the grip, and the 16 directions of attraction operate through you without your effort."
      },
